WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.876
A brand-new gadget is about to launch, and you get to set the price.

2
00:00:04.156 --> 00:00:05.027
High, or low?

3
00:00:05.307 --> 00:00:08.759
Both can be smart. It depends on who you want to win over first.

4
00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:11.321
Option one. Price skimming.

5
00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:14.593
Start high to capture the early adopters, the people who

6
00:00:14.593 --> 00:00:17.532
camp outside the store because they need it on day one.

7
00:00:17.812 --> 00:00:20.502
Then, as the excitement cools, lower the price

8
00:00:20.502 --> 00:00:23.250
step by step to reach the next group of buyers.

9
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.374
Option two. Penetration pricing.

10
00:00:26.654 --> 00:00:29.548
Start low to grab a big share of the mass market, fast.

11
00:00:29.828 --> 00:00:34.132
Low prices scare off competitors, and turn new customers into loyal ones.

12
00:00:35.082 --> 00:00:36.422
So when does each one work?

13
00:00:36.702 --> 00:00:39.436
Skimming fits when the product is new and special,

14
00:00:39.436 --> 00:00:41.732
and buyers will pay extra to get it first.

15
00:00:42.012 --> 00:00:44.866
Penetration fits when buyers are price sensitive,

16
00:00:44.866 --> 00:00:47.895
and selling a lot quickly lowers your cost per unit.

17
00:00:48.845 --> 00:00:51.513
Your turn. Think of the last product launch you saw.

18
00:00:51.793 --> 00:00:54.722
Was it skimming, or penetration? What's your evidence?
